''Networking and Volumes''

* Explain Docker networking. <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker network">docker network</$button>
** Docker provides several networking drivers:
*** bridge - default network for containers to communicate with each other and the host.
*** host - containers use the host's networking directly.
*** overlay - for multi-host networking.
*** macvlan - for assigning a MAC address to a container, making it appear as a physical device on your network.

''How do you persist data in Docker?''

<$button message="tm-modal" param="docker bind mount">docker bind mount</$button>

Using Docker volumes or bind mounts. Volumes are managed by Docker and are stored outside the container's writable layer, ensuring data persistence even if containers are removed.